</name></person-group><comment>editors</comment><year>2000</year><article-title>The challenge of health sector reform: What must governments do?</article-title><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Palgrave Macmillan</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050233-b006"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Brugha</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>McPake</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>What can be done about the private health sector in low-income countries</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12075370</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050233-b007"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kadama</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Montagu</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Working with the non-state sector to achieve public health goals</article-title><comment>Making health systems work: Working paper no. 2. World Health Organization</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050233-b008"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Sekhri</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>From funding to action: Strengthening healthcare systems in sub-Saharan Africa</article-title><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><publisher-name>World Economic Forum</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050233-b009"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Sekhri</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><